   "newText": "**Implementation caution:** Build the mask from every source-color cell, preserve its offsets from the motif bounding-box top-left, scan all in-bounds translations, and require exact background-color matches at mask cells only. Union painted mask cells across matches; never paint intervening bounding-box cells. Check dimensions/row transcription carefully. One additional demo and zero wrong submissions were used on this instance.\n\n## Task task-ebbd340b — recolor the trailing background of left-edge rows\n\n**Rule inferred and verified by accepted test:** In rows where the foreground run/object begins at the left edge, find the rightmost foreground cell (the final non-background cell in that row) and recolor every cell strictly to its right with color `1`. Leave the foreground, all cells before/within its rightmost extent, and all other rows unchanged. If the foreground reaches the right edge, there is no tail to recolor. The uniform background may be `0`, `7`, or `8`; the visible foreground can be `8` (test/demo 1) or `9` (demo 2).\n\n**Evidence:** Test bars on rows 1 and 16 ended before the right edge, so their zero tails became `1`; row 10 reached the edge and stayed unchanged. Demo 1's affected rows began with 8s and had a scattered 8-pattern ending at column 8, so only the background suffix after it became 1; another such row reached the right edge and was unchanged. Demo 2's row of 9s began at the left edge and ended before two background-8 cells, which became 1. An interior 8 stripe in demo 1 (row 3) was not transformed, so the left-edge condition is important.\n\n**Application:** Inspect each row independently. Only transform rows whose colored pattern touches column 0; stop at the rightmost colored cell and replace the suffix with `1`. Preserve dimensions and everything else. The test was accepted with zero wrong submissions (two demos requested)."
